; The x64 unwinder's imports, resolved from ntdll.dll by name.
;
; xwin's kernel32.lib routes RtlCaptureContext, RtlLookupFunctionEntry and
; RtlVirtualUnwind through api-ms-win-core-rtlsupport-l1-1-0.dll, an apiset
; the Xbox app container does not provide: the package installs and the
; loader refuses activation (observed as 0x80270300 / 0x8027015B on xllama,
; Xbox OS 26100.8866). KERNELBASE cannot take them — the console's own
; KERNELBASE export table (read from a crash dump) does not list the family.
; ntdll.dll exports all three, is loaded in every process, app container
; included, and is not apiset-versioned. The exception machinery reaches for
; them in any x64 image with unwind tables — no application code involved.
;
; build.sh turns this into an import library with llvm-dlltool and places it
; beside appcontainer-pointers.lib, before kernel32.lib, so these names
; resolve here and everything else stays where xwin put it.
LIBRARY ntdll.dll
EXPORTS
    RtlCaptureContext
    RtlLookupFunctionEntry
    RtlVirtualUnwind
